    were not flagged as missing workspace = true.
- finding_id: I2
  title: 'FieldErrorCode missing #[non_exhaustive]'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: 'No phase mentioned FieldErrorCode or #[non_exhaustive] on any enum in
    the server crate.'
- finding_id: I3
  title: Hardcoded trace_id 'none'
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote a test for meta.trace_id presence but the reviewer noted health
    generates its own UUID rather than extracting from request context. Neither phase
    flagged the hardcoded 'none' default in ResponseMeta specifically.
- finding_id: I4
  title: Zero structured logging
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: true
  caught_by: reviewer
  evidence: "Reviewer flagged [HIGH] 'No structured logging or tracing \u2014 all\
    \ src/ files. The tracing and tracing-subscriber crates are listed as dependencies\
    \ but never used. There are zero tracing::info!(), tracing::error!(), or #[instrument]\
    \ annotations.'"
- finding_id: I5
  title: Security comment claims tracing that doesn't exist
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: Reviewer noted missing tracing but did not specifically flag a SECURITY
    comment claiming logging exists when it doesn't.
- finding_id: I6
  title: Non-ASCII tenant header silently treated as missing
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No test was written for non-ASCII tenant header handling. TEA tests cover
    missing/invalid tokens but not non-ASCII header edge cases.
- finding_id: I7
  title: "CWE-209 test gap \u2014 no body assertion"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote CWE-209 tests (no stack traces leaked, no internal paths leaked,
    auth errors use generic messages) but the finding specifically notes these check
    status code without asserting on response body content.
- finding_id: I8
  title: CORS preflight test doesn't verify CORS headers
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No CORS preflight test was written by TEA, and no CORS middleware was
